    "tags": ["Vector Equation", "Line"],
    "question": "Find the vector equation of the line passing through the point $(1,2,3)$ and parallel to the vector $2\\hat{i} - \\hat{j} + \\hat{k}$. [2 marks]",
    "solutionSteps": [
      "**Step 1: Identify Given Data**",
      "Point $\\vec{a} = \\hat{i} + 2\\hat{j} + 3\\hat{k}$.",
      "Parallel vector $\\vec{b} = 2\\hat{i} - \\hat{j} + \\hat{k}$.",
      "**Step 2: Apply Vector Equation Formula**",
      "$\\vec{r} = \\vec{a} + \\lambda \\vec{b}$.",
      "**Step 3: Final Answer**",
      "$\\vec{r} = (\\hat{i} + 2\\hat{j} + 3\\hat{k}) + \\lambda (2\\hat{i} - \\hat{j} + \\hat{k})$."
    ],
    "finalAnswer": "r = (i + 2j + 3k) + λ(2i - j + k)",
    "graphRef": ""
